  "title": "Erdős Problem #42",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $M\\geq 1$ and $N$ be sufficiently large in terms of $M$. Is it true that for every Sidon set $A\\subset \\{1,\\ldots,N\\}$ there is another Sidon set $B\\subset \\{1,\\ldots,N\\}$ of size $M$ such that $(A-A)\\cap(B-B)=\\{0\\}$?",
